AquaStream360 Data Visualizer – User Guide

What This Tool Does
The Data Visualizer transforms your data into easy-to-understand charts. You provide the dataset, and it generates interactive visualizations, allowing you to explore trends, patterns, and distributions without modifying the original data.
Access: The Data Visualizer is available from multiple modules whenever data visualization is required, including Weather Data, Data Analysis, Simulation Results, and more.
________________________________________
Getting Started – Step by Step
Step 1: Opening the Tool
You can open the Data Visualizer in two ways:
1. From the Main Welcome Window
•	Click the “Data Visualizer” button.
•	The tool opens empty.
•	You need to import your data using the “Import More Data” button.
2. From Other AquaStream360 Modules
•	Opened from Water Engineering, Weather, or Data Analysis tools.
•	Your data is already loaded automatically.
•	You see it immediately in the pattern list on the right—no import needed.
________________________________________
Step 2: Understanding the Interface
The window is divided into two main areas:
•	Left panel: Big chart area where your visualizations appear.
•	Right panel: Controls, pattern list, and statistical information.
________________________________________
Step 3: Check Your Pattern List
•	If names are listed → data is already loaded.
•	If empty → you need to import data.
________________________________________
Step 4: Importing Data
Click “Import More Data” → choose your file.
Supported file types:
•	Excel (.xlsx, .xls)
•	CSV (.csv)
•	Text (.txt)
•	JSON (.json)
What happens after import:
•	Each column becomes a “pattern”.
•	Column names appear in the list on the right.
•	Select any pattern to view it as a chart on the left.
________________________________________
Step 5: Selecting a Pattern
•	Click a name in the list.
•	The chart appears immediately.
•	If data was passed from another tool, no import is needed.
________________________________________
Step 6: Choosing Chart Types
Use the dropdown at the top of the left panel to select:
•	Line Chart – shows changes over time or index
•	Bar Chart – compares values
•	Scatter Plot – shows individual points
•	Histogram – groups numbers into ranges
•	Pie Chart – shows percentages
________________________________________
Step 7: Smoothing Your Data (Optional)
If your chart looks jagged:
1.	Go to “Advanced Smoothing” on the right.
2.	Select a smoothing method (start with Gaussian).
3.	Adjust the slider:
o	Left → less smooth
o	Right → more smooth
4.	The green line updates in real time.
________________________________________
Step 8: Understanding Statistics
The Pattern Statistics box shows:
•	Number of data points
•	Average (mean)
•	Minimum and maximum values
•	Standard deviation, skewness, and kurtosis
________________________________________
Step 9: Additional Features
•	Analyze Trend → detailed trend and statistical analysis
•	Show Box Plot → display data distribution visually
•	Change Background Color → personalize chart colors
•	Predict Values → estimate values for future points
________________________________________
Step 10: Saving Your Work
Click “Export All” → choose a format → save file.
Available formats:
•	Excel (.xlsx)
•	CSV (.csv)
•	HTML (.html)
________________________________________
Important Notes
1.	If “Import More Data” is not visible → data was already loaded from another tool.
2.	Clicking a pattern name → instantly updates the chart.
3.	Original data is never altered; all changes are for visualization only.
4.	If opened from the Water Engineering module → “Replace Pattern with Smoothed Pattern” lets you save smoothed data back to your network model.
________________________________________
Quick Workflow
1.	Open the tool.
2.	Check the pattern list.
3.	If empty, import your data.
4.	Click a pattern name.
5.	Select chart type.
6.	Smooth or adjust settings if needed.
7.	Save your chart or export the data.
________________________________________
Tip: Click around and explore—everything updates in real time. You can’t break anything.

